From: BananaOS Duo Lite maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sm6125: let Venus control the vcodec hardware trigger

The HFI v4 Venus driver explicitly switches the generic power domain between
software and hardware control while sequencing codec clocks. HW_CTRL instead
hands control to hardware automatically and does not install set_hwmode_dev,
causing the driver to fall back to legacy wrapper-register control. Match the
HW_CTRL_TRIGGER contract used by the same-generation SC7180 driver, and log
successful generic handoff once for hardware validation. Reset fix pending
on-device validation; this is not a claim of resolved streaming stability.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm6125.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm6125.c
@@ -257,7 +257,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "vcodec0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.flags = HW_CTRL,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
 
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
@@ -561,6 +561,8 @@
 	}
 
 	core->hwmode_dev = true;
+	if (!ret)
+		dev_info_once(core->dev, "vcodec power handoff uses genpd hwmode\n");
 	return ret;
 
 legacy:
